NimbyTack (Tack) - original work by Jeff Fabish for NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp.
Defines four Paper subclasses and six user actions on the vanilla DayZ 1.30 action framework
(Bohemia Interactive); depends on NimbyNotes (Scrawl) from the same pack; no third-party mod code.

Changes, newest first.
- October 21, 2026 (Tack plan v0.13, fix round after the Part B in-game run, branch study/tack-t013-t014):
  - TK-P10: the roughSurfaceOffsetMeters default moves from 0.06 to 0.08 (Jeff). No config version
    bump: a version 2 file keeps what it holds (a hand-set 0.06 and the old default cannot be told
    apart), a fresh profile takes 0.08.
  - NIMBY-T-015 (plan T17): the pin is refused when the physics hit stands more than 15 cm
    (NimbyTackRules.PHYSICS_DEPTH_LIMIT_METERS, a code constant) in front of the view hit along the
    outward normal; exactly 15 cm and every negative depth pass. Reason token physics-ahead on the
    client pin-check line and the server refuse pin line (probe-detail=depth=<d> limit=0.15
