  - Config write-back (version 1 to 2 upgrade, and the defaults of a missing file) goes through
    config.json.tmp: saved, read back, version-checked, copied over the file, deleted, then the file
    is read once more; a failure logs "config <upgrade|defaults> not written; step=<save|validate|
    copy|verify>" and leaves the file as it was (shared rules 6; EnSystem.c:528,531). A file whose
    version is above the build's logs "config newer than this build; left as written".
